1308 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 572 0 R
/T (our location along the field. While most teams only use 3 odometry pods, we added a 4th dead wheel to gather additional data. This improved accuracy allowed us to navigate complex splines during auto, saving time during intake & shooting and increasing scoring.)
/E (our location along the field. While most teams only use 3 odometry pods, we added a 4th dead wheel to gather additional data. This improved accuracy allowed us to navigate complex splines during auto, saving time during intake & shooting and increasing scoring.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
1309 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 572 0 R
/E (Encoders in odometry pods can sometimes break, greatly skewing localization data. We account for the risk of inaccurate encoders within the parallel wheels by checking the difference in their readings, and using just one of them if the difference is too large. Taking a weighted average also allows us to minimize individual encoder errors.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
